   ```\n   - **Fallback**: If transfer fails, revert to random restart. Handle `RuntimeError` in solver.\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**:  \n   - Feasibility Checks:  \n     ```python\n     assert all(0 <= x <= 1 for x in h),\"Bounds violated\"\n     tolerance = 1e-5\n     assert np.abs(sum(h) - n/2) <= tolerance,\"Sum constraint violated\"\n     ```\n   - Objective Validation:  \n     ```python\n     c_valid = compute_correlation(h)\n     ```\n\n   Final code structure:\n   ```python\n   import numpy as np\n   import time\n   from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n   def enforce_sum(h, target, rng):\n       # Clip and adjust sum with random perturbations\n       pass\n\n   def random_feasible_vector(n, rng):\n       # Generate random feasible vector\n       pass\n\n   def compute_correlation(h):\n       # Fast correlation calculation\n       pass\n\n   def simulated_annealing(h, rng, T0, Tf, start_time, max_time):\n       # Time-aware SA loop\n       pass\n\n   def slsqp_optimize_one_beta(h, beta, rng, max_iter=300):\n       # Beta-adaptive SLSQP\n       pass\n\n   def run(seed, budget_s):\n       n_start = 360\n       if 'initial_h_values' in globals():\n           h_prev = np.array(initial_h_values, dtype=float)\n       else:\n           h_prev = random_feasible_vector(n_start, rng)\n       n_list = [360, 720, 1440]\n       for i, n in enumerate(n_list):\n           interpolate, enforce_sum, run_SA, refine_SLSQP_with_beta_sweep\n       return best_h.tolist(), best_c, n\n   ```",
